WEBVTT

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:06.580
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Bit of a short week, then. Can everyone hear me?</v>

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:10.779
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, but there's two of you. One's quite enough.</v>

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.109
<v Marcus Hale>That's my end, sorry. Teams and the laptop speaker.</v>

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.780
<v Marcus Hale>There. Headset's actually connected now.</v>

00:00:18.359 --> 00:00:22.210
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Jamie Brennan's absent today. Otherwise I think we're all here.</v>

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:25.350
<v Callum Reid>Yep, I'm here. Camera's off, but I'm here.</v>

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.260
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, updates first, then a few new bits. How are you getting on?</v>

00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:38.179
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, booking the contractor for the Arburg — done the prep, just the write-up left on that.</v>

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, cheers.</v>

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:50.759
<v Callum Reid>And the risk assessment for work, I've got the prep done there as well. Just the write-up left. Bit of a theme, unfortunately.</v>

00:00:51.609 --> 00:00:54.060
<v Fiona Doyle>The paperwork always outlasts the interesting bit.</v>

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:56.710
<v Sarah Okafor>Doesn't it just. Tommo?</v>

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:04.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>I've made a start on checking the guarding on the stacker. Only partway through it.</v>

00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:10.430
<v Tomasz Nowak>And that filter swap, I've had a first look. Nothing major so far.</v>

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:12.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks. Olumide?</v>

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:16.530
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Monthly fire alarm test's all done. All fine.</v>

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.099
<v Callum Reid>Nice. That's what you want to hear.</v>

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:31.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Also, Haley asked me to pass on that the new starters' training records need to come off his list. Olumide, I'm moving those over to you to sort.</v>

00:01:33.409 --> 00:01:37.609
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, I'll take over sorting the training records for the new starters.</v>

00:01:38.129 --> 00:01:39.530
<v Marcus Hale>Thanks, mate. Appreciate that.</v>

00:01:40.969 --> 00:01:43.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. New bits for today, then.</v>

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:50.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha Begum, can you order spare parts for the outfeed conveyor on Friday? Normal priority.</v>

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:55.650
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, just checking — order placed on Friday, not parts landed here on Friday?</v>

00:01:58.019 --> 00:02:00.819
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right, order placed. Not a delivery deadline.</v>

00:02:01.969 --> 00:02:07.569
<v Aisha Begum>Fine, I'll order the spare parts for the outfeed conveyor on Friday. Normal priority, got it.</v>

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:12.319
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, makes sense. Order date and delivery date get muddled so easily.</v>

00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:19.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Marc, can you chase the purchase order for the Boiler Feedwater Pump this morning? That one's fairly important.</v>

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.650
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, so chasing the PO, rather than putting another order in.</v>

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.419
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Just the chase.</v>

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.849
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll chase the purchase order for the Boiler Feedwater Pump this morning. Understood, fairly important.</v>

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:38.189
<v Tomasz Nowak>The glamorous side of engineering, that.</v>

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.800
<v Marcus Hale>Oh, living the dream. Headset on, purchase order numbers.</v>

00:02:46.289 --> 00:02:52.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Fiona Doyle, can you write up the near miss at the pick and place on two after lunch?</v>

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:57.169
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, you clipped a bit there. After lunch?</v>

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, after lunch.</v>

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:08.659
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, yes. I'll write up the near miss at the pick and place on two after lunch.</v>

00:03:11.129 --> 00:03:15.680
<v Callum Reid>You're clear again now, Sarah. It went a bit robotic for a second.</v>

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:24.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Good old Teams. Haley, one more for you: can you check the guarding on the door switch on two next Tuesday? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.139
<v Marcus Hale>Next Tuesday, yeah? Not this Tuesday?</v>

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Next Tuesday, yes. Top priority please for that check.</v>

00:03:33.939 --> 00:03:39.539
<v Marcus Hale>Okay, I'll check the guarding on the door switch on two next Tuesday. Got the priority.</v>

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.580
<v Aisha Begum>Bank holiday's thrown my sense of the week completely.</v>

00:03:43.919 --> 00:03:48.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Same here. Right, that's the work covered. Anything else before we finish?</v>

00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:57.259
<v Tomasz Nowak>Only that the charity bake sale on Friday is apparently very competitive this year. Not a work item, just slightly alarming.</v>

00:03:59.719 --> 00:04:02.169
<v Fiona Doyle>Competitive how? Are people measuring the cakes?</v>

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.330
<v Tomasz Nowak>Wouldn't surprise me. Mine would fail the visual inspection.</v>

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:11.500
<v Callum Reid>Never mind visual. What's the hardness reading?</v>

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:19.329
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you — I was going to say, depends whether it's cake or a test piece.</v>

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.959
<v Marcus Hale>With his baking, both.</v>

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:25.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this turns into a materials review...</v>

00:04:26.839 --> 00:04:30.339
<v Aisha Begum>Strong start to a Tuesday. We've already got cake tolerances.</v>

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.490
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cruel, this team. Absolutely cruel.</v>

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:38.600
<v Sarah Okafor>And on that note, thanks everyone. We'll leave it there.</v>

00:04:39.649 --> 00:04:40.850
<v Fiona Doyle>Cheers, all.</v>

00:04:42.759 --> 00:04:43.959
<v Marcus Hale>Cheers.</v>

00:04:45.279 --> 00:04:46.480
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Thanks, bye.</v>
